1
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:22,800
She lost him, but she found herself. And somehow that was everything.

2
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:39,600
Taylor Swift: The 1989 World Tour - Live is a music
film directed by Jonas Åkerlund.

3
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:56,400
Filmed in front of 76,000 fans at the ANZ Stadium in Sydney, Australia, "The 1989 World Tour Live" captures Taylor Swift's
entire performance while also mixing in behind-the-scene, rehearsal, and special guest footage from her 1989 Tour.

4
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:13,200
Self, played by Taylor Swift.

5
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Self - Musical Guest, played by Mick Jagger.

6
00:31:40,800 --> 00:31:46,800
Self - Musical Guest, played by Wiz Khalifa.

7
00:36:57,599 --> 00:37:03,599
Self - Musical Guest, played by Ally Brooke.

8
00:42:14,400 --> 00:42:20,400
Self - Musical Guest, played by Camila Cabello.

9
00:47:31,200 --> 00:47:37,200
Self - Musical Guest, played by Dinah Jane.

10
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Taylor Swift: The Eras Tour is a 2023 American concert film produced by the
singer-songwriter Taylor Swift and directed by Sam Wrench.

11
00:58:04,800 --> 00:58:10,800
It documents the Los Angeles shows of the Eras Tour (2023–2024), Swift's sixth
headlining concert tour and the highest-grossing tour of all time.

12
01:03:21,600 --> 01:03:27,600
Swift struck an unprecedented distribution agreement with AMC Theatres and Cinemark Theatres
for the film after negotiations with the major film studios fell through.

13
01:08:38,400 --> 01:08:44,400
Filming took place in August 2023 across three shows at SoFi Stadium in Inglewood, California, with a
budget of $10–20 million and SAG-AFTRA permitting production to proceed amidst its 2023 strike.

14
01:13:55,199 --> 01:14:01,199
Swift announced the film later that month, catching studios off guard and causing the release dates
of several films that had been set for release on or near October 13 to be moved.

15
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
The unconventional release strategy was a topic of media discourse; many journalists and industry personnel praised Swift's move to bypass the
studios to partner with theatres and opined that the move defied the traditional producer–distributor–exhibitor model of releasing films.

16
01:24:28,800 --> 01:24:34,800
The film premiered at the Grove in Los Angeles on October 11, 2023,
and was released to theaters worldwide on October 13.

17
01:29:45,600 --> 01:29:51,600
It was met with significant ticket demand, amassing a record $37
million on its first day of pre-sales in the U.S.

18
01:35:02,400 --> 01:35:08,400
and over $100 million in total global pre-sales.

19
01:40:19,199 --> 01:40:25,199
The Eras Tour became the highest-grossing concert film of all time,
earning $267.1 million in its limited theatrical run worldwide.

20
01:45:36,000 --> 01:45:42,000
It received acclaim from critics, most of whom praised the direction,
spectacle, energy, and Swift's artistry and showmanship.

21
01:50:52,800 --> 01:50:58,800
An extended cut of the film, subtitled (Taylor's Version), includes performances withheld from the
theatrical edit and was released on the streaming service Disney+ on March 14, 2024.

22
01:56:09,600 --> 01:56:15,600
A second concert film recorded at the tour's final show on December 8, 2024, in
Vancouver, was also released on Disney+ on December 12, 2025.

23
02:01:26,400 --> 02:01:32,400
Subtitled The Final Show, the film was directed by Glenn Weiss and featured The Tortured Poets
Department act that was incorporated into the tour's setlist after Wrench's film was released.

24
02:06:43,200 --> 02:06:49,200
The film explores themes of concert, pop star, pop culture, pop singer, singer.
